def longest_consecutive(nums):
    s = set(nums)
    best = 0
    for x in s:
        if x - 1 not in s:
            length = 1
            while x + length in s:
                length += 1
            best = max(best, length)
    return best
```
Each value is stepped over by the inner loop at most once overall (only from its run's start), so total work is O(n).

